    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n70994" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νομοθετ-ικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>relating to legislation, legislative,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				657a
			</span></i>: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ -κή</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέχνη</span>) <i>legislation,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Grg.</u>
				464c
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				520b
			</span></i>, al. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Cod.Just.</u>
					1.4.34.14
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Just.
				<u>Nov.</u>
				4.3
			</span></i>
			<u>Intr.</u>, <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				4.26
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of persons,
				<i>fitted for</i> or <i>skilled in legislation,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>EN</u>
				1180b24
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνδρες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Jul.
					<u>Caes.</u>
					320b
				</span></i>
			.</div>
